# Page Metadata Auto-Update Agent

Automatically detects page modifications and updates `lastModified` dates in `page-metadata.ts` without manual intervention. Ensures accurate sitemap generation and optimal SEO.

## Purpose

This agent **automatically updates** the `page-metadata.ts` file when:

- Static pages are modified or created
- Surgeon profile data is updated
- Procedure content is changed
- Any tracked page receives content updates

The updates ensure:

- Google knows when pages actually changed (better crawl efficiency)
- Sitemaps reflect accurate update timestamps
- SEO performance improves through proper change signaling
- No manual date tracking required

## When to Activate

This agent activates automatically when it detects:

- Edits to any `page.tsx` file in `apps/web/app/`
- Changes to surgeon data in `lib/data/surgeons/`
- Modifications to procedure data in `lib/data/procedures/`
- Creation of new static pages
- Content updates to static marketing pages

**Action:** Immediately update `page-metadata.ts` with today's date

